	"descriptionMarkdown": "# j's Nuclear\n## Kovarex\n### Starter Kovarex and Fuel Cell ramp-up\n- Optimized for fast ramp-up of centrifuges with 50% of U-235 going towards fuel cell production as soon the first centrifuge is filled with 40x U-235\n- Note: First Kovarex-generated U-235 will only be returned once ALL centrifuges are fed with one set of inputs!\n### Kovarex Extension\n- Can be FORCE Printed to the right side of the centrifuge array, (so belts are properly turned and removed by the lamp)\n- Adds additional Kovarex bandwidth once the first array is fully saturated.\n- Note: Due to optimization for fast ramp-up, the additional array will only be fed once the first array is fully operational, so the adding the extension early does not make much sense.\n## Tileable Reactors\n- 10 tile x 292 tile footprint, tileable on the long edge\n- The horizontal large power poles are chunk-sized (32 tiles) \n- Fuel cells are LogiBot-Supplied\n- One standard water Pump can supply max 2 prints of FULL 2x2!\n- water supply in the middle via underground pipes\n#### Starter 1x2 Reactor\n- Provides the smallest possible footprint for a 2x1 reactor design, good to kick-start power production but keeping the future footprint of the setup\n#### Minimal 2x2 Nuclear\n- Provides the optimal ration of a 2x2 reactor for heat consumption and power generation possible.\n#### FULL 2x2 Nuclear\n- Provides the maximal possible heat consumption for late game with multiple prints of the 2x2, due to additional neighbor bonuses\n\n# Changelog\n## 2026-07-04\n- Fixed kovarex (wires were messed up, addded more storage, now fuel only starts when the first centrifuge has 40 U-235 is filled in)\n- Removed kovarex extension BP since it is currently not extensible\n- Replaced hazard concrete with stone bricks, since that tend to be in the network, to avoid robo logistic blinkings\n## 2026-06-19\n- First release of 2x1, 2x2 single, 2x2 full, kovarex + extension, shopping list",
